First, she sold a third at the greenhouse. So that's x/3. Then she sold 2 more to the red house. Then, after that, she had some left, and she sold half of that at the orange house, leaving her with 5. 

Let me try to write this as equations. After selling x/3 at the greenhouse, she has x - x/3 left. That simplifies to (2x)/3. Then she sells 2 more at the red house, so subtract 2 from that. So now she has (2x)/3 - 2. Then she sells half of that at the orange house. So she sells ( (2x)/3 - 2 ) / 2, which means she has half of that remaining. 

So after selling at the orange house, the remaining vacuum cleaners would be ( (2x)/3 - 2 ) / 2 = 5. 

